{"kind":"assert","text":"The documentation citation gate is red on current main and was red before this work started. Running go test -count=1 -run TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord ./internal/docset/ at ca2836ab itself, and at my head 14fdfb2b, produces the identical set of five newly-fatal citations: 076ced4d, 821e2369, 88cc2168, bfcf6197 and e6080d3d, each reported as \"retired with no successor, so the pages naming it rest on a withdrawn pointer\", and each not recorded in citation_baseline.txt. They are named by eleven pages including docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/concepts/actors.md, docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md and the mcp reference set. The cause is bare supersessions taken during the ca2836ab merge step against artifacts those pages cite: a bare gs supersede withdraws the pointer without naming where the behaviour went, so every page anchored to it goes fatal rather than flaring. Recorded here as evidence, not as a claim on the repair: the retirements are codex-authored, so only codex or a ratifier can publish covering successors at those paths, and that work needs its own request."}